Q: RN Refresh parent screen after navigating back from particular screens A: <p>I think you can use the React navigation lifecycle events like this</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>function Profile({ navigation }) {
  React.useEffect(() =&gt; {
    const unsubscribe = navigation.addListener('focus', () =&gt; {
      // Screen was focused
      // Do something
    });

    return unsubscribe;
  }, [navigation]);

  return &lt;ProfileContent /&gt;;
}
</code></pre>
<p>here is the documentation: <a href="https://reactnavigation.org/docs/navigation-lifecycle#react-navigation-lifecycle-events" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://reactnavigation.org/docs/navigation-lifecycle#react-navigation-lifecycle-events</a></p>

Q: How to add entry points at runtime A: <p>Entry points are properties of <code>Distribution</code>s, and the <code>importlib.metadata</code> machinery uses <code>MetaPathFinder</code>s to find distributions. So without a “real” distribution to attach the entry points, we need to create a <code>MetaPathFinder</code> that finds a custom <code>Distribution</code> which has our entry point.</p>
<p>My example also shows how to make the entry point point to a module variable (here the <code>Needle</code> class) using <code>__name__</code>:</p>
<pre class="lang-py prettyprint-override"><code>import sys
from importlib.abc import MetaPathFinder
from importlib.metadata import Distribution, EntryPoint, EntryPoints
from types import MappingProxyType
from typing import TYPE_CHECKING, override

if TYPE_CHECKING:
    import os
    from collections.abc import Iterable, Sequence
    from importlib.machinery import ModuleSpec
    from importlib.metadata import DistributionFinder, SimplePath
    from types import ModuleType


class Needle:
    &quot;&quot;&quot;The thing we want to point our entry point to.&quot;&quot;&quot;


class MyDist(Distribution):
    # internal machinery needs `.name` to be unique,
    # so let’s use one that no other distribution has
    metadata = MappingProxyType(dict(Name=__name__, Version=&quot;0.0.0&quot;))

    @override
    def read_text(self, filename: str) -&gt; str | None:
        return None

    @override
    def locate_file(self, path: str | os.PathLike[str]) -&gt; SimplePath:
        raise RuntimeError

    @property
    @override
    def entry_points(self) -&gt; EntryPoints:
        name = &quot;...&quot;
        group = &quot;...&quot;
        ep = EntryPoint(name, f&quot;{__name__}:Needle&quot;, group)
        return EntryPoints([ep])


class MyFinder(MetaPathFinder):
    def find_spec(
        self,
        fullname: str,
        path: Sequence[str] | None,
        target: ModuleType | None = None,
    ) -&gt; ModuleSpec | None:
        return None

    def find_distributions(
        self, context: DistributionFinder.Context | None
    ) -&gt; Iterable[Distribution]:
        &quot;&quot;&quot;Find fake distribution.&quot;&quot;&quot;
        yield MyDist()

sys.meta_path.append(MyFinder())
</code></pre>
